        to the voter rolls when they become eligible to vote.



        To vote in an election, you must be registered by the applicable
        voter registration deadline. Residents should review their voter
        information regularly and update their registration whenever they
        move, change their name, or wish to update their party affiliation.





      Register to Vote





      Check Registration Status





      Update Registration Information (Name, Address, Party Affiliation)





      Track Mail Ballot








Use VoteInMA to register to vote, verify your registration status,
update voter information, locate your polling location, and track ballots.



Visit VoteInMA






     📚 Massachusetts Election Resources 


        Access official election information, voter guides, and statewide voting resources.



       Massachusetts Elections Division


     📕 The Big Red Book 


        The Big Red Book is a nonpartisan voter guide that provides information
        about candidates and ballot questions to help voters make informed
        decisions before Election Day.



        Printed copies of the Big Red Book are available at Hopedale Town Hall
        in the Town Clerk's Office and Finance Department, as well as at the
        Hopedale Council on Aging. Large-print copies are also available for
        residents who prefer an easier-to-read format.





       View the Big Red Book Online



        The Big Red Book also includes a Voter Checklist that can be printed,
        completed at home, and brought with you on Election Day as a personal
        reference while voting.



